<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss SMI market cap up one bln Sfr, new weights.</title>
<headline>Swiss SMI market cap up one bln Sfr, new weights.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The market capitalisation of firms in Switzerland's blue-chip Swiss Market Index (SMI) increased by around one billion Swiss francs in the second half of 1996 to 403.5 billion francs, the Swiss Exchange said.</p>
<p>The registered shares of Novartis, the life sciences group formed by the merger of Sandoz AG and Ciba-Geigy AG, have the heaviest weight in the index with 23.57 percent.</p>
<p>The increased capitalisation and the exercise of options caused a slight adjustment in the weighting of shares in SMI from mid-1996 to January 3, the exchange said.</p>
<p>The exchange provided following details: Market value is based on share price on December 31, 1996 and number of shares on January 3. Weighting in percentage.</p>
